{
  "//": "ORBIT HOP - you orbit a planet automatically. Tap to let go along your current heading; whatever planet you reach captures you. Reach the green one.",
  "//host": "There is no array lookup here, so 'which planet am I orbiting' is a number and the host position is selected by nested ifElse over three constants. That is the whole reason this game has exactly three planets.",
  "//release": "relT is a cooldown since release. Without it the player is recaptured by the planet it just left on the very next frame, because it is still well inside that planet's capture radius.",
  "//engine": "Expressions cap at 32 RPN tokens. ifElse(falseValue, trueValue, condition) reads its condition LAST. Every equation reads the previous frame's values.",
  "//planets": "p1 (100,250) r34, p2 (215,140) r30, p3 (325,265) r34 = the goal.",
  "header": {
    "apiLevel": 7,
    "width": 400,
    "height": 400,
    "profiles": 513,
    "contentDescription": "Orbit Hop: tap to leave orbit and fly to the next planet"
  },
