  "//levels": "Clearing a level means being captured by the green planet. All three planets are functions of `level`, so the layout changes every level while the capture radius shrinks. Drifting too long without a capture costs a life and rebuilds the same level.",
  "//fail": "`hit` here is 'flying for more than 220 frames without being captured', which reuses the same grace-gated death machinery as the other games.",
  "//geometry": "The three planets sit 120 degrees apart on a circle rotated by level, so they are always well separated. Independent trig per planet overlapped planets 1 and 2 at level 1, 29px apart against a radius of 26."
